+// that is writable and executable at once. The way out is to map the buffer through ONE
+// alias with svcMapProcessCodeMemory and flip its permissions between Perm_Rw and
+// Perm_Rx. That fits oaknut's model -- a single address to emit and to execute -- because
+// dynarmic already calls unprotect() before emitting and protect() before executing (see
+// backend/arm64/address_space.cpp). It is the same mechanism melonDS uses.
+//
